			{
				"type": "Comment",
				"start": 0,
				"end": 462,
				"data": "\n\tA text after a block element keeps the space before the inline element that follows it:\n\t`text3 text4 <span>x</span>` renders `text3 text4 x`. Prettier deletes that space\n\t(`text3 text4<span>x</span>`, which renders `text3 text4x`) — a content change — whenever the\n\ttext's predecessor is a block element, for a one-word text too, and whether or not the run is the\n\tfragment's first. A tag or a component after the same text keeps its space under both.\n"
			},
			{
				"type": "Text",
				"start": 462,
				"end": 464,
				"raw": "\n\n",
				"data": "\n\n"
			},
